# Figma reference code

When the user says to copy from Figma, take a reference from Figma, match the Figma design, or take colour codes from Figma, look **only** in:

```
C:\Users\sriva\Downloads\TYNG APP (Copy)
```

Do not ask where the Figma files are, and do not look in any other folder.

## What is inside

- A Figma Make export: React + Tailwind (Vite) under `src/`.
- Player screens live in `src/app/components/player/` (for example, Home is `HomeScreen.tsx`).
- Shared colours are constants near the top of each screen (for example `GREEN = '#8CF000'`, `ORANGE = '#FF7A00'`, `DARK = '#111827'`, `MUTED = '#6B7280'`). Exact sizes, radii and shadows are in the Tailwind classes (for example `rounded-[26px]`, `text-[10px]`, `shadow-[0_8px_28px_rgba(17,24,39,0.20)]`).

## How to search it

The folder is outside the workspace and the Glob tool times out on it, so use the shell:

```powershell
cd -LiteralPath "C:\Users\sriva\Downloads\TYNG APP (Copy)"
rg -l -i "SECTION TITLE TEXT" src
rg -n -i "SECTION TITLE TEXT" src\app\components\player\HomeScreen.tsx
```

Then read the matching component with the Read tool.

## Applying it in this app

- This app is Ionic/Angular with SCSS, so translate the Figma Tailwind classes into SCSS. Never copy React code directly.
- Figma uses sample data. Wire every value to real API data, and tell the user about any Figma value that has no backend data behind it.
